    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-16 (round 6).**\n\n**Symptom.** On hypergumbo's own self-analysis, 3 paths each have **2 `file`-kind Symbol nodes** instead of one:\n\n```\npackages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_websocket.py    (2 file symbols)\npackages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/serve.py    (2 file symbols)\npackages/htrac-frontend/src/ws-client.ts    (2 file symbols)\n```\n\nAll three are paths that the WebSocket linker processes (one server-side handler, one TS client, one Python test fixture).\n\n**Inspection of `ws-client.ts`'s two file symbols:**\n\n```\n# Symbol 1 (correct, from js-module-linker-v1):\nid=typescript:packages/htrac-frontend/src/ws-client.ts:module_file:1:ws-client\n  name=ws-client\n  language=typescript\n  origin=js-module-linker-v1\n  path=packages/htrac-frontend/src/ws-client.ts          (relative ✓)\n  stable_id=typescript:packages/htrac-frontend/src/ws-client.ts:module_file:1:ws-client\n\n# Symbol 2 (phantom shadow, from websocket-linker-v1):\nid=websocket:/home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo/packages/htrac-frontend/src/ws-client.ts:1-1:file:file\n  name=ws-client.ts\n  language=javascript   ← WRONG — file is TypeScript\n  origin=websocket-linker-v1\n  path=packages/htrac-frontend/src/ws-client.ts          (relative)\n  span=1-1\n  stable_id=None        ← schema violation\n```\n\n**Root cause.** `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/websocket.py:553-556` constructs a Symbol with `kind=\"file\"`:\n\n```python\nsymbols.append(Symbol(\n    ...\n    kind=\"file\",\n    ...\n))\n```\n\nWhen the file already has a Symbol from the language-side analyzer (Python via py.py, TypeScript via js-module-linker, etc.), the WS linker creates a parallel shadow node rather than reusing the existing Symbol or attaching meta to it.\n\n**Three derived bugs from the same line:**\n\n1. **Duplicate file nodes.** Self-analysis produces 3 extra file Symbols.\n2. **Wrong language attribution.** WS linker stamps `language=\"javascript\"` even for `.ts` files. Cross-references to \"the WebSocket TS client\" silently end up grouped under JS.\n3. **`stable_id=None`.** Schema-conformance violation alongside the other Symbol-stamping gaps already filed as INV-sopon (\"19/21 linkers missing Symbol.origin\" — websocket is one of them). This adds `stable_id` to the list of fields the WS linker omits.\n\n**Relationship to existing tracker items.**\n\n- `WI-fozoh-…` (`done`) closed the broader \"732 duplicate file nodes\" issue. The fix presumably addressed analyzer-side duplication but missed linker-side phantom creation. Today's 3-dup count is a 99.6% reduction but not 0.\n- `INV-sopon-…` (filed round 2) — websocket is one of the 19 affected linkers; that item covers the missing `origin` stamp. This finding is **adjacent** (same linker, sibling fields) but distinct in symptom (phantom Symbol creation, not just missing field).\n\n**Fix proposal.**\n\nTwo viable approaches:\n\n1. **Don't create the phantom file Symbol.** The WS linker should look up the existing file Symbol via the analyzer's symbol registry and reuse it. If the Symbol doesn't exist (file unparseable), skip the WS edge rather than synthesize a file. This is the cleanest fix.\n\n2. **If synthesis is required, fix the metadata.** When the WS linker MUST emit a file Symbol (e.g., for cross-language WS edges where one side has no language analyzer), it should:\n   - Resolve `language` from the file extension (`.ts` → typescript, not javascript)\n   - Use relative paths (the path field is already relative in this case — only the `id` field has absolute path)\n   - Stamp `origin = \"websocket-linker-v1\"` and `stable_id` per the existing analyzer convention\n\nRecommended: (1) for cleanliness; fall back to (2) if there's a legitimate synthesis case.\n\n**Tests.** Add a regression test asserting `len({n for n in nodes if n.kind == \"file\" and n.path == X}) == 1` for any path. This is an invariant (one file Symbol per file path) that should hold across all linkers.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/websocket.py:520-560` (synthesis sites)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/ir.py:204-359` (Symbol docstring)\n- `WI-fozoh-bahos-…` (done) — original 732-dup fix\n- `INV-sopon-…` (filed round 2) — sibling linker-symbol-stamping gap\n\n**Notebook reference.** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05162026_0438.md` Round 6 section."  # 6289
    fields:  # 6289
      statement: "Each file path must have exactly one Symbol with kind='file'. Linkers must not synthesize phantom file Symbols when the language analyzer has already produced one. When a linker DOES synthesize a Symbol, it must set language correctly (from file extension), use relative paths, and stamp origin and stable_id per the existing analyzer convention."  # 6289
      root_cause: "packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/websocket.py:553-556 constructs Symbol(kind='file', language='javascript', stable_id=None) without checking whether the language analyzer has already produced a file Symbol for the path. Produces 3 duplicate file nodes on hypergumbo self-analysis (test_websocket.py, serve.py, ws-client.ts). The .ts file gets language='javascript' (wrong). WI-fozoh's 732-dup fix addressed analyzer-side duplication; linker-side phantom creation slipped through."  # 6289
