  message: "Re-applying state change after auto-pr rebase clobber (per output-capture-long-running-playbook hazard).\n\nRoot cause of the 2026-05-19 no_move identified and fixed by WI-hifol (PR #3819, commit c926c2e5e3, merged to dev).\n\nWebSocketPattern.file_path was populated from absolute Path objects yielded by find_js_ts_files / find_python_files, so _make_file_id(language, pattern.file_path) produced ids embedding /home/.../packages/.../file.py — while the orchestrator's synthesize_file_symbols_for_dangling_edges and the language analyzers emit canonical ids embedding repo-relative paths because analyze/all_analyzers.py::run_all_analyzers normalizes every Symbol path before linkers run. The two id shapes never collided so dedup-against-ctx.symbols silently missed every cross-producer case; the post-linker path-normalization sweep at cli.py:7244-7247 fixed Symbol.path but not Symbol.id.\n\nFix: linkers/websocket.py::link_websocket now mirrors the orchestrator's exact normalization algorithm (forward-slash + repo_root prefix-strip, NO symlink resolution) on every pattern.file_path after pattern collection. Verified by self-analysis dogfood (2026-05-19): 3 -> 0 websocket-origin duplicate file Symbols.\n\nStatus moved to satisfied. awaits_bakeoff_validation tag stripped. INV-zadum and INV-dajaf METAs can both close now (all 11/11 children either satisfied or downstream-closed)."  # 9aa3
